<title>FRANCE: Usinor's unit invests in Turkey.</title>
<headline>Usinor's unit invests in Turkey.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sollac, a unit of Usinor Sacilor, said on Wednesday it was building in partnership with local metal packaging producer Sarten a tinplate service centre in Turkey.</p>
<p>The centre, Sollac Metal Emballaj, will start operations in May 1997 in Manisa near the town of Izmir, the statement said.</p>
<p>It will serve small and medium sized packaging producers.</p>
<p>It already owns a 10 percent stake in Turkish cold-rolled mill Borcelik.</p>
<p>Sollac delivered 1.1 million tonnes of tinplate in 1996.</p>
</text>
